  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "$P(A)=p$, $P(B)=\\frac{3p}{2}$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{2}{3}$. Find $p$ if:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$p=\\frac{4}{15}$.",
          "worked": "Since the events are mutually exclusive, $P(A\\cap B)=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cup B)&=P(A)+P(B)\\\\\\frac{2}{3}&=p+\\frac{3p}{2}\\\\\\frac{2}{3}&=\\frac{5p}{2}\\\\p&=\\frac{4}{15}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$A$ and $B$ are independent",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$p=\\frac{1}{3}$.\n\nUse independence in the addition rule and reject the root greater than 1.",
          "worked": "Independence gives $P(A\\cap B)=P(A)P(B)=\\frac{3p^2}{2}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cup B)&=P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B)\\\\\\frac{2}{3}&=p+\\frac{3p}{2}-\\frac{3p^2}{2}\\\\4&=15p-9p^2\\\\9p^2-15p+4&=0\\\\(3p-1)(3p-4)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $p=\\frac{1}{3}$ or $p=\\frac{4}{3}$. Since $p=P(A)$ is a probability, reject $\\frac{4}{3}$. Therefore $p=\\frac{1}{3}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      }
    ]
  },
